                                        "examples": []
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "04afff32-9b37-455d-bf9a-3b35b467e611",
                        "source_entry_id": "a8809002-1474-366e-aaaf-b4007c2fa42a",
                        "source_sense_id": "e14d3b66-a320-3a2d-8bd9-981ab452aa79",
                        "target_lang_word": "whole enchilada",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "whole enchilada",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "1d8cfe2f-7f9f-3aca-9745-d630070aca68",
                                        "entry_id": "a59b6671-469a-3843-8964-4684e4852602",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "All of something or a group of related things taken in totality."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "idiomatic",
                                            "informal"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "686eb454-23ab-43ea-8e34-a32b6ff2aaf2",
                                                "sense_id": "1d8cfe2f-7f9f-3aca-9745-d630070aca68",
                                                "text": "They need a fall guy for the whole enchilada."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "6835c0be-e2a8-417f-9a16-0db21ca7035e",
                                                "sense_id": "1d8cfe2f-7f9f-3aca-9745-d630070aca68",
                                                "text": "\"I want the wife, the kids, the house, the dog, the whole enchilada,\" he said in his rapid-fire way of talking."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "ba49a848-3aa0-48a2-8ed5-1d47f7609d03",
                                                "sense_id": "1d8cfe2f-7f9f-3aca-9745-d630070aca68",
                                                "text": "Your job as a software developer is not to simply slam out code, but to deliver the whole enchilada."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "0e5ac918-644c-4c1a-877f-2874e910e2ed",
                                                "sense_id": "1d8cfe2f-7f9f-3aca-9745-d630070aca68",
                                                "text": "It is only by loving all of ourselves (the whole enchilada!) that unconditional love of self is possible."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "8cb1bcec-4fff-480d-88ac-b04e5584e333",
                        "source_entry_id": "a8809002-1474-366e-aaaf-b4007c2fa42a",
                        "source_sense_id": "e14d3b66-a320-3a2d-8bd9-981ab452aa79",
                        "target_lang_word": "whole nine yards",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": []
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "19e012f7-1c8c-4347-ba1b-d389564dfc24",
                        "source_entry_id": "a8809002-1474-366e-aaaf-b4007c2fa42a",
                        "source_sense_id": "e14d3b66-a320-3a2d-8bd9-981ab452aa79",
                        "target_lang_word": "usual suspects",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "usual suspects",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "3a7d9da6-4ee2-3077-8022-f757767d60fd",
                                        "entry_id": "0afd39ed-99de-32c5-87ea-4f2e1caaf2fa",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "The people, often scapegoats, routinely arrested in response to a crime."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "ironic",
                                            "often",
                                            "plural",
                                            "plural-only"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "b329b3ee-b7d0-41f0-960f-c2fc025ca170",
                                                "sense_id": "3a7d9da6-4ee2-3077-8022-f757767d60fd",
                                                "text": "Major Strasser has been shot... round up the usual suspects."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "a90d33b6-3636-3771-aeed-ee24138a4a68",
                                        "entry_id": "0afd39ed-99de-32c5-87ea-4f2e1caaf2fa",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "The people or things that would be routinely expected to appear in a particular context."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "broadly",
                                            "informal",
                                            "plural",
                                            "plural-only"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "3e9d6c5d-14b5-413b-b2df-1503074d8484",
                                                "sense_id": "a90d33b6-3636-3771-aeed-ee24138a4a68",
                                                "text": "I think the eco-utopian picture … is an unlikely outcome. I generally avoid over-population arguments. But there’s no question we’re in population overshoot. The catch is we’re not going to do anything about it. There will be no policy. The usual suspects: starvation, war, disease, will drive the population down. There’s little more to say about that really, and it’s certainly an unappetizing discussion, but it’s probably the truth. In any case, we’re in overshoot and we face vast resource scarcities. That’s it. The “usual suspects” are already doing their thing as worldwide food prices go up and peoples on the margin begin to suffer and starve."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "2be873f7-8b4d-4b2f-bfeb-8a85ab4866bf",
                                                "sense_id": "a90d33b6-3636-3771-aeed-ee24138a4a68",
                                                "text": "And yet a quiet campaign is in the works to secure landmark protection for the 46-story limestone and glass tower. It is not being led by the usual suspects, like preservationists, community groups or politicians."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "6b4d03f4-6e96-4674-abdb-e351430b9ee2",
                                                "sense_id": "a90d33b6-3636-3771-aeed-ee24138a4a68",
                                                "text": "It was - to be only a little bit unfair - all the usual suspects at the Paris demo. Trotskyite students chanting against the patriarchy; anarchists; grizzled veterans of '68; plenty of pensioners; theatre-workers. In other words the regular left-wing alphabetti-spaghetti."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
